        "How the reference image is aligned with the target video - Image 1 (from Shot 1) is aligned with the 0.00 second mark of the target video; Image 2 (from Shot 1) is aligned with the last frame mark of the target video.\n\nIntegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] A live-action, cinematic, still shot of a portrait composition starting with the precise pose, hand placement, framing, lighting, and color identified in Figure 1. The camera remains completely still - no pan, tilt, push, zoom, truck, roll or handheld movement - background objects, walls, lights and composition never move or change. The character's lip movements are synchronized with <Audio 1>. His eyes remain on the camera, natural blinks and slight changes in expression passing over his face. His head remains level and centered at the same angle and in the same position, with only barely noticeable slight adjustments, never turning, tilting, nodding, or tilting. Keep hands below chin, relaxed and half-open, never grasping, pointing, holding objects, crossing or covering face. His movements then narrow and stabilize, and by the end of the shot he has achieved the exact sitting position, hand position, mouth shape, gaze, framing, lighting, and color identified in Figure 2.",
